  "description": "Calibration approaches the body as a field of forces held in a structured balance. Soft volumes gather around a rigid axis, swelling where pressure accumulates and tightening where it is restrained. Rather than concealing tension, the structure translates invisible force into contour, rhythm and a provisional anatomy.\n\nEchoing the logic of the hydrostatic skeleton, the form emerges through the dependency of softness and constraint. Neither fixed nor freely expanded, it remains suspended between compression, resistance and release.\n\n“In short, the form of an object is a ‘diagram of forces.’”\n D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form, 1917",
